The present graphics abilities of 3.0e release nethack are rather
impressive.  With the following, the vt100 can be set to give the
special characters of a not equal for a web, a solid small diamond
for a kitchen sink, the greek letter pi for a throne, and the
British pound mark for an altar.  I for one second Roger Gonzalez's
sentiments that a separate string for each object and monster is
probably better and that almost everybody has a terminal that can
highlight a region.  However, the future seems to be with x-windows
and a more complete solution lies in this direction.
===================================================================
as=                             \EH^B   ^N
ae=                             \EH^C   ^O
ti=                             ^N      \E)0
===================================================================
Object/Terminal        deflt   Wyse50  Vt100
===================================================================
solid rock
vertical wall           |       \m6    \mx
horizontal wall	        -       \m:     \mq
upper left corner       -       \m2     \ml
upper right corner      -       \m3     \mk
lower left corner       -       \m1     \mm
lower right corner      -       \m5     \mj
cross wall              -       \m8     \mn
upward T wall           -       \m0     \mv
downward T wall         -       \m=     \mw
leftward T wall         |       \m4     \mu
rightward T wall        |       \m9     \mt
vertical beam           |       \m6     \mx
horizontal beam         -       \m:     \mq
left slant              \       \\     \\
right slant             /       /     /
door                    +       +     +
floor of a room         .       .     \m~
corridor                #       \m;     \ma
stairs up               <               <
stairs down             >               >
trap                    ^               ^
web                     "               \m|
pool or moat            }               }
fountain                {               {
kitchen sink            #               \m`
throne                  \               \m{
altar                   _               \m}
ladder up               <
ladder down             >
vertical drawbridge     #
horizontal drawbridge   #
